    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In consequence, if the problem (5.1) is defined in a Lie group G , then the scheme Sh of order p is conjugate to a method that preserves the Lie group structure up to order 2p+1 .This is so up to order 2p+2 if Ψh is symmetric-conjugate and the order p is even, due to the particular structure of Kh in that case [5]. On the other hand, if Ψh is symmetric-conjugate and its order p is odd, then the resulting AC method is time-symmetric and of order p + 1 ."
  }, {
